nd atom but when it comes to  design the carl goes its own way  the opel designer says the very dynamic  front and headlights draw the eye  towards the vehicle side here you find  the typical sickle shaped characteristic  of opal it's supported by these very  dynamic lines up here which make the car  look even more compact and give it its  own unique character  unlike the two-door atom the coral is a  four-door creating 940 liters of trunk  space was a challenge for the designers  giving the cars small dimensions  stefan notes that they might have to  shorten the seats or arrange things  differently than they would in a larger  car center consoles or storage  compartments might be closer together  than they are in the insignia or astra  yet it works  he's 1.76 meters tall and with the right  adjustments can sit comfortably in the  driver's seat or in the back  the coral has a manual 5-speed  transmission our test car boasts the  most expensive trim package and costs  upwards of thirteen thousand euros in  germany opel says that this little car  also uses little fuel  still stiff on stresses that the carl is  a four-door model with seating for five  that makes it a more family-friendly and  more of an all-rounder than the atom  which targets a younger and more  feminine segment  here opel's targeting older more  conservative buyers who have to mine  their money more  those looking for a lifestyle car will  likely opt for the atom the corsa is a  somewhat larger more complete vehicle  with a choice of several body styles and  variants  the coral is opal's entry-level model  but nonetheless very complete  starting this summer with the coral the  atom and the corsa in its stable opal  will boast the strongest lineup of super  minis in its history and among the  latest on the market  audi debuted its compact suv q3 in the  autumn of 2011. now the german car maker  has given its niche offering a refresh  and refined the performance version the  rs q3  the rs exhaust syste