king it go  to the max this kind of power comes at a  price of course not just with a purchase  but with a running cost as well  bmw is rolling out its latest  convertible just in time for spring the  new 2 series rag top is 7.2 centimeters  longer than its predecessor otherwise  its proportions are typically bmw with a  long hood and wheelbase and broad toe  at the touch of a button the soft top  opens and shuts in just 20 seconds even  at speeds of up to 50 kilometers an hour  the top of the line version is the bmw  all-wheel drive m235i x drive with a 240  kilowatt engine  fiat's giving its family minivan the  doblo a new look the headlights are  better positioned to prevent cracks from  flying grit and clumsy parkers the  streamlining has been improved too but  the car is still available in two  lengths allowing customers to configure  it into a seven seater with room for  four thousand liters of luggage  prices start at seventeen  800 euros for the 70 kilowatt basic  model with a gasoline engine and short  wheelbase a top flight longer 99  kilowatt doblo sells for nearly 25 000  euros  the porsche moves peacefully through the  snow on a tranquil winter's day  quiet isn't something most people  associate with the famed german sports  car  roaring engines and a thirst for fuel  are more likely to come to mind  our tester chris question says the  silence is made possible by an electric  motor under the hood this vehicle was  porsche's first plug-in hybrid  though there are now hybrid cayennes and  918 spider super sports cars the  panamera was porsche's first plug-in  hybrid the luxury sedan requires four  hours to recharge its batteries but that  power supply entails a sacrifice of  nearly a third of the panamera's 435  liter trunk space  the sc hybrid system output is high  acceleration is rapid and the sedan has  a top speed of 270 kilometers an hour  just what you'd expect from a porsche  but what's unexpected is the car's low  fuel consumption porsche says it